    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) stand out as our must-start anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta; crucially, his high score is bolstered by Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a key upside for his stolen base potential in our category-starved environment. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** faces a high-xERA opponent in Bradford, and his ability to leverage a 19% SP skill advantage and a favorable park pushes him into elite territory. **Jackson Merrill** (69.57) also provides significant value, as his strong platoon advantage against Bibee mitigates the risks of a challenging SP matchup.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the bottom of the order, where **Coby Mayo** (43.08) just narrowly missed the cut. While **Coby Mayo** offers a solid baseline, he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon efficiencies of **Dominic Smith** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are keeping a close watch on **Andy Pages** (47.54) and **Heliot Ramos** (45.90); both possess dynamic SB potential against their respective starters, but their efficiency scores are hampered by tough matchups against elite arms like Henderson and Cease. Even with these pitchers presenting high xERAs, **Kyle Tucker** (51.47) remains in our utility slot, though his floor is somewhat restricted by the current pitching environment. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a void in our power production. Owners should note that the sub-50 scores for **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Dominic Smith** suggest we are operating with a cautious approach to game-cap preservation today. We are prioritizing high-contact, high-speed profiles like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** to navigate the volatility of these matchups, especially with the scarcity of stolen bases keeping our lineup construction strictly tied to daily efficiency thresholds.",
